# breadcrumbs repository .gitignore (for the tool's own repo)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.DS_Store

# The repo's own .project-memory/ store IS committed: this project dogfoods
# its own tool (superseding the earlier never-commit rule — see
# dec_20260815_the-tool-s-own-repo-commits-its-own-memory-store). The managed
# block below keeps private/ and index/ local, same as any target project.

# But never commit a packet regenerated by running `resume` on a fixture
# (it is a rebuildable projection; CI regenerates it transiently).
fixtures/**/.project-memory/generated/resume-packet.md

# ...EXCEPT fixtures 8, 9 and 11, which commit a packet on purpose:
#   - fixture 8 ships a deliberately-stale packet (wrong inputs_hash) so `audit`
#     drift detection has something to catch;
#   - fixture 9 ships an accurate packet as the CLI-less cloud-fallback artifact;
#   - fixture 11 ships the packet two machines must agree on byte-for-byte.
!fixtures/fixture-08-packet-stale/.project-memory/generated/resume-packet.md
!fixtures/fixture-09-cloud-fallback/.project-memory/generated/resume-packet.md
!fixtures/fixture-11-multi-machine/.project-memory/generated/resume-packet.md

# >>> breadcrumbs managed block (managed by `crumb init`) >>>
.project-memory/private/**
.project-memory/index/**
!.project-memory/index/README.md
.project-memory/generated/*.local.md
.project-memory/generated/*.tmp
# <<< breadcrumbs managed block <<<
